                <pb facs="0213" n="115" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg115"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.11/1130: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Canton</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jenkins</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Canton</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-05-14T12:00:00+08:00">May 14, 1930—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received
                        May 14—9:05 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring to my telegram of May 9, 3 p.m. I am glad to be able to report that I
                    have just received a telegram dated May 10 through Hong Kong from General Huang
                    Shao-hung promising an armed guard to escort the American missionaries out of
                    Kweihsien. Department and Legation informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jenkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
